{
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "about": "Rough outlines of the world's major present-day forests, for scattering tree glyphs on the globe (scripts/build-decorations.ts). Natural Earth has no forest layer, so these were drawn by hand: each is a coarse polygon of longitude/latitude points a few degrees apart, placed by eye to follow the forest's broad present-day extent as shown on biome maps (such as WWF's terrestrial ecoregions). They were not traced from any dataset and are deliberately loose. Outlines may run over sea, lakes and mountains: glyphs are only placed on land, outside lakes, and mountain and desert regions take priority over forest. 'glyphs' gives the mix of tree glyphs drawn in each forest (weights).",
